  "_note": "Golden vectors of the EvNode 0x76 transaction encoding on XO mainnet (chain 3223), computed by the TypeScript SDK. execHash is the executor signing hash; encodeSigned is the signed envelope with the fixed fee-payer and executor signatures of the test. Every case's transaction and envelope were also re-encoded with Foundry's cast to-rlp, which gives the same bytes. Checked against XO's production sponsor with sign-only requests (POST https://sponsor.xo.market/v1/sponsor/sign, which broadcasts nothing) on 2026-10-30: a fresh executor key signed the case's transaction, the sponsor recovered that executor from its own signing hash (so its executor hash equals execHash), and its fee-payer signature recovers to the sponsor 0x1237eDde231af0CF5b45cA924A366Aa5ccEFf7a9 over keccak256(0x78 || executor || the RLP-encoded payload fields, with an empty fee-payer slot and no list header). The sponsor signs only zero-value calls to XO's contracts, so the cases call USDC and ConditionalTokens. Per case: C1_transfer, C2_batch, C4_accesslist and C7_batch32 are checked by the sponsor. C6_boundary is checked by the sponsor; the 0x7f and 0x80 boundary values are its fee fields, because a call value must be zero. C8_sighighbit's transaction is checked by the sponsor; its high-bit executor signature appears only in encodeSigned, which only the cast to-rlp re-encoding checks. C3_create is not independently checked: the sponsor's policy refuses contract creation, so only the cast to-rlp re-encoding covers it. C5_maxvalues is not independently checked against mainnet: its chain ID is 2^64-1, not 3223; it does not depend on the chain, and its bytes are unchanged from those the sponsor's reference Rust encoder emitted for this transaction. In every case, the tail of encodeSigned (the fee-payer signature and the executor's yParity, r and s) is checked only by the cast to-rlp re-encoding.",
